{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas","id":938645,"title":"101 Court Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-27T23:39:57-07:00","id":938645,"title":"101 Court Ideas","content":"Since Court Creation is going to be big in 2e, and they're moving away from Seasonal Courts being the default, let's come up with some ideas for courts, their laws, their Bulwarks, and so on. <br /> <br /> 1. A Freehold set up as a &quot;republic of pirates&quot;, with the courts being a group of pirate crews, each with a distinctive Jolly Roger and approach. Their bulwark is quite simple- they have to commit acts of piracy, consisting of attacking a ship and taking at least one item of value from it. Law in the Freehold is based on a modernized form of the Pirate Code- each Court has a Captain and a Quartermaster, both of whom are elected and can be impeached by a vote. All plunder is to be equally shared, with the captain never receiving more than twice as much as the lowest member. Crew members are to have no quarrels &quot;at sea&quot; (interpreted to mean whenever the Court is in power), but are to settle their disputes with a duel &quot;on land&quot; (interpreted to mean whenever the Court is not in power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T11:59:44-07:00","id":938995,"title":"","content":"I came up with one which was based on the legend of King Arthur with each position named after a character within the legends and the passing of the crown being done through a convoluted mock betrayal by one of the King's most trusted friends (chosen by the wyrd ahead of time and expected to betray the king at the moment where it would have the most impact, though usually it never resulted in the death of the king). Almost all of the court members were expected to follow the code of chivalry (the exception was the court spy, the morgana if I remember right).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T14:06:43-07:00","id":939121,"title":"","content":"3. A freehold I've come up with (The Limelight Freehold) is one that bases itself with history as well as theater. All four courts within the freehold are based on History - the Bone court is based on personal history and mistakes, and how to improve on them; the Coal court is based on societal history and living as they used to; the Dust court is based on making history while being as obscure as possible in recorded history; and the Paint court is about living in a romanticized version of history, just as paintings (and other media) would have it. Every year each of the courts must make a stage production based on the history of the area they are in, be it about the city, the people who founded it or even on the fiction produced within it, with the leader of the freehold being the director of the current stage production. However, the production must be successful, plagiarism free and not a repeat of a previous production in order for the Wyrd to accept it and the leadership to pass to the next leader. Members of the other courts are invited to participate in the current production though. Should all four productions be complete before the year is out, the court leaders form a council instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T16:00:49-07:00","id":939198,"title":"","content":"I wrote a serious of courts based on Edgar Allen Poe stories and poems. One court acted out the Masque of the Red Death, and took on the role of Revelers, and at years end performed a mock murder of the sitting King. One Court worked in the style of Montresor, from the Casque of Amantillado, changed rulers via temporary entombment, and made a point of being very vengeful people. The third court took on the role of Raven, and made it a point to be sneaky information gatherers, and once a year would gather and have a competition over who had the juiciest secret. My fourth Court is based on the poem Lenore, playing the role of wailing mourners and they write one eulogy a year for a fellow, living, changeling; the most written of Changeling is offered the title of Lenore for a year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:16:37-07:00","id":939222,"title":"","content":"5. A UK-based freehold founded by a clique of hobbyist wargamers when they escaped together, themed after Warhammer Fantasy's Winds of Magic, seeing as how they have &quot;been purified of Dhar.&quot; There's only four Courts (since changelings, by nature, are imbalanced in their favor), but they pay respect to all in hopes of keeping the Qhaysh Ward (their Bulwark) intact. They view their Glamor feeding as using humans to focus the Winds through and into themselves. The College of Azyr studies the abstract nature of concepts and fate, and focuses their Wind through Curiosity, trading their knowledge (however misleading) for power. To them falls the task of supplicating Hysh by transforming knowledge into law and moral rightness. The College of Ulgu studies the nature of illusion and deceit to better outwit the True Fae, and focuses their Wind through Confusion, feeding on the spiraling eddies that surround the perplexed and lost. To them falls the supplication of Chamon, using their illusions to clarify what is concrete and objective, and to give the world inspiration to work the static into new forms. The College of Ghyran studies life and the process of change, and focuses their Wind through Growth, the sense of accomplishment that comes from realizing one is better than before. To them falls the grim duty of supplicating Shyish, for death must follow life, and eternity without change is stagnation. And finally, the College of Agshy studies passion and war, and focus their Wind through Vengeance, the sense of a grudge in the process of repayment. To them falls the duty of supplicating Ghur, for war is the foundation of so much of nature, and animals run on passion. Every year, the Deans meet and select two to control what the League of the Redeemed Magi will have as its agenda. One, the Archmage, is a mighty changeling like any other, to control the intellectual aspects of their duty-but the other, the Duke Malleus, is a mortal skilled in lower but safer and saner arts. To her falls the task of organizing the League's military and secret police-for the Huntsmen know what story the League draws from, and they have taken it as a dare...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T17:20:51-07:00","id":939224,"title":"","content":"Presumably they've mastered Goldspinning, because they need it to afford all those expensive models.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T04:17:47-07:00","id":939437,"title":"","content":"The Flavor Courts are a collection of Changelings who's personalities and names are derived from different spices, seasonings, textures and tastes. The Spicy Court is the most out going and energetic of the bunch, and contains most of the Freehold's warriors. The Creamy Court is more relaxed and prefers to keep things running as smoothly as possible to avoid stress and confusion. The Sweet Court are the P.R managers who maintain a facade of innocence and purity for the rest of the Freehold. And the Sour Court is full of tricksters and cynics who's sense of humor is satisfied at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> The Flavor Courts keep the Fae out of their Freehold by regularly holding private dinner parties which the True Fae are not invited too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2016, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T07:34:04-07:00","id":939521,"title":"","content":"The Star Trek Courts.<br /> <br /> The Ferengi Alliance Court- Emotion Greed<br /> The Federation of Planets Court- Emotion Hope<br /> Klingons Empire Court- Emotion Wrath<br /> Cardassion Union Court- Emotion Obligation<br /> Romulan Star Empire Court- Emotion Paranoia<br /> Orion Sydicate- Emotion Lust","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T08:27:52-07:00","id":939549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=939521#post939521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Star Trek Courts.<br /> <br /> The Ferengi Alliance Court- Emotion Greed<br /> The Federation of Planets Court- Emotion Hope<br /> Klingons Empire Court- Emotion Wrath<br /> Cardassion Union Court- Emotion Obligation<br /> Romulan Star Empire Court- Emotion Paranoia<br /> Orion Sydicate- Emotion Lust</div> </div> </div> </div>No Vulcan Court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T09:18:13-07:00","id":939577,"title":"","content":"Vulcans are members of the Federation, they can be a Noble Entitlement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T10:50:33-07:00","id":939639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=939437#post939437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Flavor Courts are a collection of Changelings who's personalities and names are derived from different spices, seasonings, textures and tastes. The Spicy Court is the most out going and energetic of the bunch, and contains most of the Freehold's warriors. The Creamy Court is more relaxed and prefers to keep things running as smoothly as possible to avoid stress and confusion. The Sweet Court are the P.R managers who maintain a facade of innocence and purity for the rest of the Freehold. And the Sour Court is full of tricksters and cynics who's sense of humor is satisfied at the expense of others.<br /> <br /> The Flavor Courts keep the Fae out of their Freehold by regularly holding private dinner parties which the True Fae are not invited too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume they have quite a few Knights of the Tongue (objectively the best Entitlement) in their ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T12:13:50-07:00","id":939697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=939639#post939639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume they have quite a few Knights of the Tongue (objectively the best Entitlement) in their ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That, and maybe some others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Iron Chef (bestowed upon mortals who serve the Courts.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Lord / Lady of the Buffet (position of high status / nobility)<br /> <br /> <br /> Eating Champion (given in recognition for great deeds of heroism)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Spice of Life (King / Queen of the Spicy Court)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Rich Pudding (King / Queen of the Creamy Court)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Cherry on Top (King / Queen of the Sweet Court)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sour Patch Kid (King / Queen of the Sour Court)<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:43:54-07:00","id":939761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=939697#post939697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Spice of Life (King / Queen of the Spicy Court)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Scoville Units... A troop of Spicy Warriors.<br /> <br /> Why didn't I think of that before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:39:33-07:00","id":939833,"title":"","content":"When Courts were first revealed in the 2e development blogs, I started fiddling with the idea of a Freehold that had some inspirations from Hogwarts, and had seem cross-over stuff with Beast.<br /> <br /> Centuries ago, the Freehold of Edinburgh was under siege from the Bodach, an exceptionally powerful Fae Lord. The changelings petitioned a great Dragon who dwelt in human form (a powerful-like-whoa Ugallu) for aid, but he refused, until the Bodach kidnapped his human daughter to Arcadia and turned her into a wyvern. Furious, the Dragon declared war on the Bodach and his servants. He rallied the changelings of Edinburgh, and made four of them his generals. Together, the Dragon and the changelings beat back the Bodach, and the Dragon and his generals ruled the freehold. Upon his death, the Dragon's generals became the first monarchs of the courts, and his daughter became the Dragon Queen.<br /> <br /> The Dragon Monarch acts as a sort of High Monarch for the freehold. He or she is chosen from among the monarchs, though the Dragon Monarch typically names one of them as an heir to try and prevent infighting. The Dragon Monarch has final say over the rule of the freehold, but usually makes decisions in concert with the other Monarchs, and leaves the Monarchs to handle matters within their own courts. He or she also gives final approval on the Monarchs' candidates for Knight, and personally selects two Knights to be First Knight and First Dame of the freehold. The Dragon Monarch does not personally rule over a court, though the other Monarchs and title holders could be said to be his/her court in some ways.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bear Court:</b> Representing the Dragon's claws, the Bear Court follows the Emotion of Perseverance. Known for their unwavering loyalty and tireless work ethics, Bear Courtiers rarely boast about their triumphs or seek out rivalries with members of other courts, but are often negatively stereotyped as simple-minded and unambitious. Their gem is the diamond, and their metal is iron.<br /> <br /> <b>The Eagle Court: </b>Representing the Dragon's wings, the Eagle Court follows the Emotion of Awe. Known for staggering intellects and wits, Eagle Courtiers always seek greater fame, greater renown, and greater wisdom, but can be incredibly competitive and even willing to betray their friends and hinder competitors to get the upper hand. Their gem is the sapphire, and their metal is bronze.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lion Court: </b>Representing the Dragon's jaws and roar, the Lion Court follows the Emotion of Courage. Known for their courage, chivalry, and boundless nerve, Lion Courtiers are always to enter the fray or fight against an injustice, but can be short-tempered glory-hounds, sanctimonious martyrs, and defiant rule-breakers. Their gem is the ruby, and their metal is gold.<br /> <br /> <b>The Viper Court: </b>Representing the Dragon's fangs and body, the Viper Court follows the Emotion of Disdain. Known for their cunning and willingness to help each other, Viper Courtiers rarely take direct action against threats, gaining a reputation as dishonorable blackguards and elitist snobs. Their gem is the emerald, and their metal is silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 07-29-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T18:48:24-07:00","id":939894,"title":"","content":"One idea I've had is that of a popular Egyptian Freehold that's the local equivelent of the Seasonal Courts, tying themselves to the ebbs and flows of the Nile, whose life-giving waters serve as their Bulwark. The Courts would be<br /> <br /> Aketo(Flooding): Court of Anticipation, They who rush, the Warrior's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Peret(Growing): Court of Toil, They who tend, the Worker's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Syumuu(Harvesting): Court of Catharsis, They who reap, the Court of Priests","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T07:04:33-07:00","id":940068,"title":"","content":"Two Freehold Ideas I've come up with:<br /> The Courts of Las Vegas were once the traditional Seasonal Courts, but the Spring and Summer Courts overtook the others by far, and their Bulwark failed. Nearly overwhelmed by the True Fae and their Huntsmen, the members of the Freehold forsook tried-and-true knowledge and reinvented themselves through Wits, Skills, and Luck, redefining themselves as the Suit Courts: The Diamond Court of Want, The Spade Court of Fury, the Club Court of Apathy, and the Heart Court of Melancholy. Their Bulwark involves many games of chance and the testing of each Courts\u2019 Champions through those games.<br /> <br /> The Courts of Bremen based themselves around the story of the \u201cMusicians\u201d of Bremen, finding kinship with the four animals who fled their masters and combined their talents to defend themselves and make their fortune. The Rooster Court of Pride, the Judges, are the sages and inquisitors who master communications and expose corruption; The Cat Court of Cunning, the Witches, are the mystics and scholars who study the secrets of the Hedge and the unknown; the Hound Court of Loyalty, the Devils, are the warriors and guards who pursue and destroy threats to the Freehold; and the Donkey Court of Resolve, the Giants, are the artisans and workers who forge and work to support the Freehold and bolster its power. The Courts submit to the authority of a council of their Monarchs who direct their efforts towards greater goals. The Bulwark consists of various processes to determine new Monarchs: The Roosters hold an election amongst themselves, the Cats seek to unveil the greatest discovery, the Hounds participate in a series of duels, and the Donkeys work to craft the most wondrous creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12200-blitzmentalist","name":"BlitzMentalist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T08:14:01-07:00","id":940085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=939894#post939894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea I've had is that of a popular Egyptian Freehold that's the local equivelent of the Seasonal Courts, tying themselves to the ebbs and flows of the Nile, whose life-giving waters serve as their Bulwark. The Courts would be<br /> <br /> Aketo(Flooding): Court of Anticipation, They who rush, the Warrior's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Peret(Growing): Court of Toil, They who tend, the Worker's Court<br /> <br /> \u2022Syumuu(Harvesting): Court of Catharsis, They who reap, the Court of Priests</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really like to see a more detailed write-up of this, especially since I might possibly use this court system for the Changeling side of Age of Azar.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:48:59-07:00","id":940120,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I actually had some doubts about replacing the seasonal-default system with the more freeform create-a-court system, but you guys have given me so many cool ideas that now I'm totally on board with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:19:19-07:00","id":940153,"title":"","content":"It is certainly a lot of effort, but yeah, I like this freeform system too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T11:24:06-07:00","id":940155,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Courts of the Diwatas</b></u><br /> Several of the indigenuous Courts in the Philippines are tied not to seasonal cycles or geographic locations. Instead, they are tied to local Dreamers, exiled True Fae who have been transformed by their interactions with humanity to a greater extent than the so-called Charlatans. These Gentry represent many of the precolonial gods of the country, and the courtiers' veneration of them forms the basis of their Bulwark. A notable example of this system are the Courts of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maria_Makiling\" target=\"_blank\">Maria Makiling</a>, who draw their identities from the legends attributed to her. <hr />The concept of the Dreamers came from the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/949353-goblin-chronicles-2e\">Goblin Chronicles Fan Supplement</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T14:59:56-07:00","id":940273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=940120#post940120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I actually had some doubts about replacing the seasonal-default system with the more freeform create-a-court system, but you guys have given me so many cool ideas that now I'm totally on board with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still plan to stick for Seasonal Courts of majority Freeholds in Europe and Americas ( i.e. defaults in game settings there ). But when I will have greater/cooler ideas for local Courts, could make them in place of Seasonal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Pitty we still do not have proper 2E write-up of Seasonal Courts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T20:56:52-07:00","id":940429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=940273#post940273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pitty we still do not have proper 2E write-up of Seasonal Courts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834952#post834952\">Claire's writeup notes</a> are anything to go off of, the Seasonal Courts still have a fair amount of regional variation upon their core themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T19:52:33-07:00","id":941002,"title":"","content":"I had the Australian Sydney Courts be based loosely around the seasons but be warped into the Celestial Courts;<ul><li><b>Court of the Moon</b> - Which exemplified curiosity, change, liminality, potential and the seasons of autumn and spring. They make goblin vows with Full-Moons.</li> <li><b>Court of the Stars</b> - Which exemplified greed, inevitability, endurance, self-determination, and the season of winter. They make goblin vows with Midnight.</li> <li><b>Court of the Sun</b> - Which exemplified passion, creation, drama, fate, and the season of summer. They make goblin vows with Noon.</li> </ul>And the central coast of Australia got a court system based around the Past, Present, and hoped Future of the region:<ul><li><b>Court of Sands</b> - Which exemplifies excitement, standing out, socializing, manipulation, entertainment, blue, blue angel, glaucus atlanticus, and the potential future of the region. As their mantle grows they become more athletic, can make goblin vows with Beaches, can get into any social event, and become one of the Illes kith. This court also grants membership to the region's kindred, parasites drifting from one event to another for easy prey, though they earn their keep my covering up the region's supernatural activity and by manipulating mortals into creating more events for the Sand Court to attend.</li> <li><b>Court of Serpents</b> - Which exemplifies regret, reconciliation, nature, learning, memory, red, red-bellied black snake, pseudechis porphyriacus, and the past of the region. As their mantle grows they become more academic, can make goblin vows with Serpent Artwork, gain perfect memory, and become one of the Antiquarian kith. This court also grants membership to the region's awakened and bound, assisting the court in gathering knowledge on the regions history and spreading knowledge that members have discovered through more effective means.</li> <li><b>Court of Spiders</b> - Which exemplifies contentment, togetherness, unity, safety, temperance, black, black house spider, badumna insignis, and the current state of the region. As their mantle grows they become more empathetic, can make goblin vows with Currently Used Spiderwebs, spiders start to guard and watch over your home, and become one of the Truefriend kith. This court also grants membership to the region's begotten and forsaken, where territory is carefully discussed and they work to keep the region's supernatural ecology relatively stable.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 08-10-2016, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:10:38-07:00","id":941170,"title":"","content":"My ideas are less developed than some here, but I've been thinking that a trio of courts based on the Dark Triad (<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_triad\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_triad</a>) would be interesting- except instead of anything so overt, they'd all mask their true natures beneath slightly more agreeable facades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T15:45:29-07:00","id":941460,"title":"","content":"The Dark Triad Courts seem interesting. I considered trying to make Courts based on the three parts of the afterlife in the Divine Comedy (Paradiso, Purgatorio, and Inferno), but couldn't figure out how to go beyond the obvious. Maybe there could be some overlap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12200-blitzmentalist","name":"BlitzMentalist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:49:23-07:00","id":941940,"title":"","content":"I had some loose ideas for a court system for a nautical community, with the courts corresponding to proximity to the water. The half-baked version is as follows:<br /> <br /> Court of the Steady Soil - attracts those who are even in temperament, grounded in tradition, seek safety. Themes: social, mercantile, nature, safety, hearth, warmth, tradition, construction, wood and earth, stone.<br /> Court of the Shifting Sands - attracts the capricious and whimsical, exemplifies adaptiveness, very responsive but not necessarily attentive, independent. Themes: whimsy, self-improvement, leisure, adaptation, sand, driftwood, hidden treasures<br /> Court of the Unforgiving Tide - attracts the hard-headed and determined, the tide is regular and powerful, and so too are its courtiers. independent and unyielding. Themes: perseverance, combat, order, obfuscation, imminent dangers, waves, waxing and waning, cycles, ships, maritime activities<br /> Court of the Bent Horizon - attracts both the academic and the adventurous, united in curiosity and wanderlust but aware of dangers of straying too far. themes: exploration, knowledge, maritime warfare, the deep ocean, shipwrecks, the occult, hidden threats<br /> <br /> Still a lot of cooking left on the idea but given the historical and metaphysical significance of the sea there's got to be a court system somewhere set up around it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:19:55-07:00","id":942941,"title":"","content":"The Courts of Glasgow follow the Seasonal style, but are additionally defined by the Miracles of St Mungo. Spring is the Bird; representing rebirth after tragedy. Summer is the Tree, the fire renewed and stronger than ever. Autumn is the Fish, representing the spoils of fear and suspicion. Winter is the Bell, mourning the dead- representing the despair of the city and the cold times spawned from the coming of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Summer; The Iron Spear, The Tree Aflame<br /> <br /> Spring; The Antler Crown, The Lazarus Bird<br /> <br /> Autumn; The Leaden Mirror, The Drowned Promise<br /> <br /> Winter; The Silent Arrow, The Mourning Bell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:30:05-07:00","id":943881,"title":"","content":"Iron Chefs as a title for mortals, clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:41:54-07:00","id":943892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzMentalist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=941460#post941460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Triad Courts seem interesting. I considered trying to make Courts based on the three parts of the afterlife in the Divine Comedy (Paradiso, Purgatorio, and Inferno), but couldn't figure out how to go beyond the obvious. Maybe there could be some overlap?</div> </div> </div> </div> You could tie them to Atheist (Inferno), Agnostic (Purgatory), Faith (Paradise), but emphasis that Inferno and Purgatory aren't evil and Paradise isn't good, but rather is ones approach to those who concider themselves &quot;spiritual&quot; Authorities.<br /> <br /> Maybe Inferno looks at Paradise and thinks they like worship a True Fae in the guise of &quot;God&quot;, so rebellen makes sense, Paradise thinks Inferno are fools as only the power of &quot;God&quot; could protect them from the True Fae, and Purgatory are just pragmatists working to better themselves without worrying about religion. <br /> <br /> Emotions Rapture (Paradise), Doubt (Inferno), Curiousity (Purgatory).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T06:34:52-07:00","id":944812,"title":"","content":"That could work (And don't worry, I wasn't going to give the Courts unambiguous morality stances.)<br /> I considered referring to them as the Nine Spheres, the Seven Levels, and the Nine Circles, since that's how the various areas were set up in the poem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12200-blitzmentalist","name":"BlitzMentalist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T21:10:22-07:00","id":956767,"title":"","content":"I have a random idea given by my friend's idea of the Gentry endorsing Pokemon GO as a way to get easier pickings at kidnapping people.<br /> <br /> The Courts of Pokemon GO were created as a response to the Gentry taking more people due to it's popularity, both in taking the fight back to the Fae, finding the most unsafe and safe routes and places and finding out the Fae's weaknesses, those who follow their fae nature to lead them to places untaken or unknown by other courts, and finally the court that would forsee harmony between the three and keep the courts in balance. Given the popularity of the game, these Courts appear wherever the game has enough reception (especially by the Changeling world) where they may sprout.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Mysticism: </b>The Frozen One, The Wise Superego. They are the Court of Logic and Wisdom, who seek out safe paths both within or without the Hedge and mark it out for the other courts to follow. They are also the masterminds and strategists who fight back against the Fae and Huntsmen with logic and reason. The court is also equally drawn to science, philosophy and technology. Their Mantle focuses on ice and cold that deafens emotions. They're known to have a huge rivalry with the Court of Valor.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Instinct: </b>The Electrifying Second, The Instinctual Ego. They are the Court of Faith and Trust, who focus upon becalming the tensions between the Changelings so they all may stand together strong against the Fae through the arts of Pledgecrafting. They also emphasize self-belief, to trust within ones own instincts. For these courtiers, their instincts are almost never wrong and though they are the least populated of the courts, they have more than a few hobgoblins they've successfully tricked into pledges. Their mantle is like that of the storm with distant thunder and lightning, for you never will know when the storm will strike. When it does however, there is no hiding from it.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Valor: </b>The Flaming Third, The Emotional Id. They are the Court of Strength and Power, who focus upon gaining strength in all forms and seeking to wield it back against the True Fae and Huntmen like the weaklings they should be. They also emphasize following your emotions, even if it leads to you burning out. After all, if you put your heart into anything you do, nothing is impossible. Their mantle is blazing, burning with fire and turning all emotions into blazing bonfires that near nobody can put out. <br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Harmony: </b>The Silver Leader, the Keepers of Ash. Unlike the other three courts, the Court of Harmony isn't exactly a fully fledged court. It's more akin to a gathering of people both within and between the three Courts of Pokemon Go who seek to keep the balance of power between the three courts to be equal, as with other courts that form by the Changelings. They are responsible for the keeping of Gyms as well as keeping the hedgespun raiments and tokens equally distributed amongst them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}